e":"Plan 93101-93108 requires byte-identical profile/signer-set carriers, both creator signatures, adjacent epochs, previous-anchor linkage, cut/QC, successor derivation, and the copied expected tuple, but never states objectId or genesisAnchorDigest equality between genesisTrust, the predecessor record, and the current record. Both existing precedents check them (packages/protocol-v3/src/index.ts:1403-1405; packages/protocol-v3/src/creator-close.ts:596-597), and the adversarial gate list at 93170-93171 assumes cross-room/cross-genesis rejection.","required_action":"Add the two explicit equalities (objectId and genesisAnchorDigest of both records equal to the genesis trust material) to the frozen authentication statement and to the 0b1 RED vectors. Disposition owner: D.110c-0b0b design text, enforced by D.110c-0b1 RED."},{"severity":"P2","title":"Bounded advance accepts caller-declared retiring refs without a stated derivation binding","evidence":"Plan 93113-93122 defines inspectBoundedCreatorTrustAdvance as a structural delta over {current,proofRefs,proposed,retiringProofRefs} after the Node/protocol owner 'has identified the current transition pair'; 'non-current' rejection is not defined, and refs alone cannot distinguish a transition pair from any other preserved ref. Closure candidates already carry scannable bytes for every ref (packages/control-plane/src/anchor-trust.ts:390-406), so kind/epoch confirmation is available.","required_action":"State that retiringProofRefs must be derived from the digests of the authenticated prior-transition CutValue/commit-QC bytes, and/or that the predicate confirms via candidates that they decode to exactly one drp-hard-epoch-cut and one drp-seal-qc bound to the retiring epoch. Disposition owner: D.110c-0b1 GREEN (control-plane boundary plus Node composition)."}],"counts":{"P0":0,"P1":1,"P2":3},"next_slice":"D110C_0B0B_CORRECTION_REQUIRED"}
